Yes, it is expected. When you set new permission classes via a class attribute or decorators, you are telling the view to ignore the default list set in the `settings.py` file.

Global default permissions are established using the `DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES` setting in your `settings.py` file. If this setting is not specified, it defaults to `['rest_framework.permissions.AllowAny',]`.

Example of setting the global default:
```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    'DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.permissions.IsAuthenticated',
    ]
}
```

